            <h3>Is the Northeast Regional from Charlottesville to Baltimore worth it? </h3>

            <p>Yes, the Northeast Regional is considered one of the best options due to its reliability, comfort, and efficiency. It allows you to travel between city centers while avoiding I-95 traffic congestion. </p>


            <h3>Can you travel from Charlottesville to Baltimore in one day? </h3>

            <p>Yes, this route is suitable for a same-day trip. With multiple departures and moderate travel times, you can travel to Baltimore and return to Charlottesville within the same day, though early departure is recommended. </p>


            <h3>What is the distance between Charlottesville and Baltimore by train? </h3>

            <p>The rail distance between Charlottesville and Baltimore is approximately 133 miles (214 km), making it a key regional rail route in the Mid-Atlantic. </p>


            <h3>Does the train have Wi-Fi? </h3>

            <p>Yes, the Northeast Regional offers free Wi-Fi onboard, though connectivity quality may vary in rural segments between Charlottesville and Washington. </p>


            <h3>Can you bring luggage on the train? </h3>

            <p>Yes, passengers may bring two carry-on items and two checked bags (up to 50 lbs each) at no additional charge. Additional bags may incur fees. </p>


            <h3>What is the difference between coach and business class? </h3>

